{
  "description": "BTPS 1.1 addresses (Protocol Specification Overview, \"Identity format\"). An address is account$domain with exactly one $. The account is a-z, 0-9, \".\", \"_\" and \"-\", 1 to 64 characters. The domain follows DNS: at least two labels of a-z, 0-9 and \"-\", each 1 to 63 characters, not starting or ending with \"-\", at most 253 characters in all; an international name in its xn-- form. Letters compare without case. An implementation accepts every \"accept\" input, refuses every \"refuse\" input, and treats each \"same\" pair as one identity.",
  "accept": [
    "alice$example.com",
    "billing.team_2-a$saas.example",
    "Billing$Vendor.Com",
    "pay$sub.domain.example.co.uk",
    "billing$xn--bcher-kva.example",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa$example.com",
    "alice$aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.example",
    "alice$aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
  ],
  "refuse": [
